        "take":  "Brown is making a supply-constraint argument at a moment when the bears are making a demand-uncertainty argument — and both can be right simultaneously. The real risk is not that AI demand disappoints; it\u0027s that the timing gap between capex and monetization creates a multi-quarter earnings air pocket before the shortage thesis pays off. For long-term holders, his framing is correct. For anyone evaluating near-term valuation, \u0027we ain\u0027t seen nothing yet\u0027 is a conviction call, not a valuation model — and those cut both ways.",
