        "take":  "Baron\u0027s story is a direct rebuke to the industry\u0027s obsession with quarterly performance attribution. The $60B return is almost entirely a function of not selling — a strategy that\u0027s nearly impossible to institutionalize because clients, compliance, and career risk all push toward activity. The broader lesson for allocators: the structural incentive to trade is the single biggest drag on long-term compounding, and most managers never escape it. Baron did, which is why there\u0027s only one of him.",
